# Both live in the base image's bundled system Python packaging tooling
# (pip/setuptools under /usr/local - never our app's own venv at
# /opt/venv, and not anything requirements.txt pulls in). `pip install
# --upgrade pip setuptools` in the Dockerfile already patches the actual
# installed copies (confirmed clean in Trivy's own per-path breakdown -
# usr/local/.../pip-26.2.1.dist-info and setuptools-84.0.0.dist-info both
# show 0 vulnerabilities); these two IDs are Trivy separately flagging
# stale metadata left behind for versions that aren't what's actually
# installed/running. Neither vulnerability's attack surface is reachable
# in production either way: this container only ever runs `uvicorn`
# serving the FastAPI app from /opt/venv - nothing here calls setuptools'
# PackageIndex (CVE-2025-47273's actual vulnerable code path) or does
# msgpack (de)serialization (GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964) at runtime. Re-evaluate
# if that ever changes.

# setuptools: Path Traversal Vulnerability in setuptools PackageIndex
CVE-2025-47273

# MessagePack for Python: Out-of-bounds read / crash on Unpacker reuse
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
